-- title:
--   The absolute row hull is centrally symmetric
-- statement:
--   For a matrix $g:Y\times X\to\mathbb R$, let $H=\mathrm{conv}\{\pm g(\cdot,x):x\in X\}\subseteq\mathbb R^Y$ be the absolute row hull. Then for every $z\in\mathbb R^Y$,
--   $$
--   z\in H\iff-z\in H .
--   $$
--
--   This symmetry is one of the requirements for the matrix body to be a symmetric convex body.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/ConvexBody.lean#L71-L87

